.TH LINTROLLER 1 2026-11-26 lintroller "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lintroller \- lint Swift sources using a compiler index
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lintroller
.BI \-\-index\-store " DIR"
.BI \-\-project\-root " DIR"
.RB [ \-\-rules
.IR ID[,ID...] ]
.br
.B lintroller \-\-help
.br
.B lintroller \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lintroller
runs SwiftLint rules on Swift source files recorded in an existing compiler
index. The
.B unused_declaration
and
.B unused_import
rules also use compiler symbol references.
.PP
Rules use built-in settings. Project settings in
.I .swiftlint.yml
are ignored. Source comments recognize
.BR swiftlint:disable ,
.BR swiftlint:enable ,
the rule selector
.BR all ,
and the scopes
.BR :previous ,
.BR :this ,
and
.BR :next .
The superfluous-disable check considers only rules selected for the run.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-index\-store " DIR"
Read the compiler index store from
.IR DIR .
Use the directory passed to
.BR "swiftc \-index\-store\-path" ,
which contains the versioned store directory, typically
.IR v5/ .
Required for a scan.
.TP
.BI \-\-project\-root " DIR"
Report findings for indexed Swift sources under
.IR DIR .
Required for a scan.
.TP
.BI \-\-rules " ID[,ID...]"
Run the specified rules. Supply a comma-separated list or repeat the option.
By default, all supported rules run, including SwiftLint opt-in rules.
See
.B \-\-help
for the supported identifiers.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and supported rule identifiers.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH INDEX COVERAGE
Use a fresh index from a successful build that includes all targets and
configurations whose references should count. Keep sources at their indexed
paths, and rebuild the index after editing or moving them.
.PP
For
.BR unused_declaration ,
indexed callers outside the project root and under
.IR .build ,
.IR .swiftpm ,
or
.I DerivedData
can count as uses. Sources at those locations produce no findings.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Each finding is written to standard output on one line in the following format.
.PP
.EX
path:line:column: error: message (rule)
.EE
.PP
Paths are relative to the project root. Line numbers and UTF-8 byte columns
start at one. Command and scan errors are written to standard error.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The scan completed without findings, or help or version information was printed.
.TP
.B 1
The scan completed with findings.
.TP
.B 2
The arguments were invalid or the scan failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
From a Swift package directory, build an index that includes test callers and
run all supported rules.
.PP
.EX
swift build \-\-build\-tests \-\-enable\-index\-store
lintroller \-\-index\-store "$(swift build \-\-show\-bin\-path)/index/store" \e
    \-\-project\-root .
.EE
.PP
Use an existing index to check only for unused declarations and imports.
.PP
.EX
lintroller \-\-index\-store /path/to/index/store \-\-project\-root . \e
    \-\-rules unused_declaration,unused_import
.EE
